---
// The table. Everything on it is the visitor's own and lives in their browser, so the page is a
// client-only island: there is nothing the server could render. Without JavaScript the page says
// what Scraps is and why it needs scripts (contract § 4.3).
import App from '../App.tsx';
import Layout from '../Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <main id="content" class="k-main">
    <h1 class="k-name">Scraps</h1>
    <App client:only="react">
      <div slot="fallback" class="k-fallback">
        <noscript>
          <p>Scraps is a table for whatever you have got: a sentence, half a thought, a doodle. Say something and it becomes a small piece of coloured paper you can pick up, restyle, write on the back of, or clip to another.</p>
          <p>The table is laid out and kept by your browser, on your device, so it needs JavaScript. Nothing you make here is sent anywhere.</p>
        </noscript>
      </div>
    </App>
  </main>
</Layout>
